# Combat damage redirected from a player to Ancient Adamantoise is combat damage dealt to the Adamantoise, not to the
# player (CR 614.1a, 120.3; the rulings: it is still combat damage), so "whenever this creature deals combat damage to a
# player" does not trigger. Bot2's Drake Hatcher (1/3) attacks Bot1 unblocked: the Adamantoise is dealt 1, Bot1 loses
# nothing, and the Hatcher gets no incubation counters. Then the Adamantoise attacks on turn 5 and Bot2 loses 8: damage to
# an opponent is no business of the redirection.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Sapphire
Black Lotus
Show and Tell
Ancient Adamantoise
Forest
Forest
Forest
Forest x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Mox Sapphire
Island
Drake Hatcher
Island
Island
Island
Island
Island x10

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Blue)
Bot1.Hand.Show and Tell.Cast
Bot1.Choose(Ancient Adamantoise)
Bot2.Choose()
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Island.Play
Bot2.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Drake Hatcher.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Island.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
[T4 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Attack(Drake Hatcher)
[T4 Bot2.Main2]
? Bot1.Life = 20
? Bot1.Battlefield.Ancient Adamantoise.Damage = 1
? Bot2.Battlefield.Drake Hatcher.Counters.Incubation = (absent)
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Attack(Ancient Adamantoise)
[T5 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot1.Life = 20
Bot2.Life = 12
Bot1.Battlefield.Ancient Adamantoise.Damage = 1
Bot2.Battlefield.Drake Hatcher.Counters.Incubation = (absent)
